<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- June 6-8.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- June 6-8.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the June 6-8 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Con Air		    $24,131,738	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. The Lost World:</p>
<p>    Jurassic Park	   $18,564,605	 $171,103,734</p>
<p>3. Addicted To Love	 $ 3,630,278	 $ 26,217,488</p>
<p>4. Buddy			$ 3,504,671	 $  ----</p>
<p>5. Gone Fishin'	     $ 2,967,041	 $ 10,508,051</p>
<p>6. Trial and Error	  $ 2,627,339	 $  9,054,715</p>
<p>7. Austin Powers:</p>
<p>    Int'l Man of Mystery  $ 2,379,075	 $ 42,884,395</p>
<p>8. The Fifth Element	$ 2,078,812	 $ 55,360,251</p>
<p>9. Breakdown		  $ 1,757,432	 $ 45,135,887</p>
<p>10 Liar Liar		  $ 1,190,265	 $168,507,740</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Con Air&quot; and &quot;Gone Fishin'&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;The Lost World: Jurassic Park&quot; and &quot;Liar Liar&quot; are released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Addicted To Love&quot; is released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;The Fifth Element&quot; and &quot;Buddy&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Trial and Error&quot; and &quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; are released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
<p>&quot;Breakdown&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
</text>
